#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(518.94pt, 790.2pt, "4 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.86pt, 82.08pt, "High-entropy alloys (HEAs), which benefit from sluggish diffusion and lattice distortion ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 102.78pt, "effects, enabling greater radiation tolerance than conventional alloys ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(402.4pt, 98.28pt, "44–46")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(422.44pt, 102.78pt, ". ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 131.48pt, "Among ceramic materials, SiC remains one of the most promising candidates for structural ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 152.18pt, "components in both fission and fusion environments. Its high thermal conductivity, corrosion ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 172.88pt, "resistance, and radiation stability make it an ideal material for cladding and structural ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 193.58pt, "applications. However, SiC is not immune to helium-induced damage. Due to its low helium ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 214.28pt, "solubility and diffusion, implanted He atoms become trapped in vacancies or pre-existing ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 234.98pt, "defects, forming stable clusters that evolve into platelets and eventually blisters ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(488.68pt, 230.48pt, "47")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(496.74pt, 234.98pt, ". The ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 255.68pt, "immobility of helium in such a matrix makes it exceptionally difficult to mitigate damage once ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 276.38pt, "initiated. ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 305.06pt, "Understanding helium transport and retention in SiC, especially in the presence of irradiation-")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 325.76pt, "induced damage, is therefore of urgent scientific and technological interest. However, the ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 346.46pt, "fundamental properties of helium behavior in solids, such as diffusion and resolution energies, ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 367.16pt, "remain poorly characterized under realistic reactor conditions. A recent study by Agarwal et al. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.86pt, 383.36pt, "48")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(78.9pt, 387.86pt, " introduced a novel approach using pre-damaged Fe subjected to self-ion irradiation. By ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 408.56pt, "combining Doppler Broadening Spectroscopy-Positron Annihilation Lifetime Spectroscopy ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 429.28pt, "(DBS-PALS) with transmission electron microscopy, they demonstrated that the presence of ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 449.98pt, "initial voids could influence cascade damage, reduce the size of large voids while increasing ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 470.68pt, "small vacancy clusters, highlighting a previously unrecognized mechanism of defect evolution. ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 491.38pt, "Inspired by this insight, ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(189.92pt, 491.38pt, "here, we introduce defect landscape engineering, the deliberate tailoring of ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 511.12pt, "vacancy cluster populations and distributions, as a strategy to control He behavior at the atomic scale. ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 530.08pt, "By designing pre-existing damage profiles, it is possible to redirect helium transport, stabilize nanoscale ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 549.04pt, "bubbles, and suppress extended defect formation. Using α-SiC as a model ceramic, we demonstrate that ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 569.02pt, "pre-existing vacancy clusters, introduced by carbon self-ion implantation ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(402.04pt, 569.02pt, "to defined damage levels ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 589.72pt, "(0.25 dpa and 0.36 dpa) to simulate reactor-relevant defect populations")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(424.36pt, 589.72pt, ", act as both sinks for ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 609.46pt, "cascade-generated interstitials and preferential traps for He. This dual functionality alters the ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 628.42pt, "thermodynamics and kinetics of He clustering, resulting in dispersed, stable nanobubbles instead of large ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 647.38pt, "platelets and cracks.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.86pt, 675.34pt, "Our integrated experimental, computational approach combines bright-field STEM, nano-")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 696.06pt, "precession electron diffraction strain mapping, elastic recoil detection analysis, depth-resolved ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 716.7pt, "positron annihilation spectroscopy, and atomistic simulations to uncover the mechanisms ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 737.4pt, "linking engineered defect landscapes to He damage suppression. Our findings establish a ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 758.1pt, "composition-independent and scalable route for tuning radiation response in ceramics. The ")
]

