#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(518.94pt, 790.2pt, "5 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.86pt, 82.08pt, "demonstrated control over He defect evolution provides a design principle applicable to a wide ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 102.78pt, "class of radiation-sensitive materials, enabling enhanced performance in nuclear, fusion, and ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 123.48pt, "other extreme-environment applications. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.86pt, 156.2pt, "Results")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.86pt, 178.88pt, "Helium Behavior as a Function of Damage and Temperature ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 199.58pt, "To evaluate the role of engineered vacancy landscapes in controlling helium defect evolution, ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 220.28pt, "we implanted α-SiC with carbon ions to introduce controlled levels of pre-existing damage prior ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 240.98pt, "to helium irradiation. The virgin α-SiC consists of larger grains, as demonstrated by the STEM-")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 261.68pt, "EDS in Supplementary Figure 1. The carbon ion energies and fluences were chosen to produce ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 282.38pt, "damage peaks at depths overlapping or slightly deeper than the helium implantation range, ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 303.08pt, "ensuring strong spatial interaction between helium atoms and defect-rich zones.")
  #line-at(454.6pt, 303.08pt, "Fig. 1 presents ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 323.78pt, "Elastic Recoil Detection Analysis (ERDA)- derived helium depth profiles under three ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 344.48pt, "conditions: (i) He implantation at room temperature (RT, black curve), (ii) He implantation at ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 365.18pt, "750 °C (red curve), and (iii) He implantation at 750 °C into SiC pre-damaged by carbon ions to ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 385.88pt, "0.36 dpa (blue curve). These are compared with Stopping and Range of Ions in Matter (SRIM)-")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 406.58pt, "simulated depth profiles for He and C ions. In undamaged samples implanted at RT and 750 ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 427.3pt, "°C, two distinct helium peaks appear at approximately 850 nm and 960 nm, suggesting partial ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 448pt, "redistribution and thermal diffusion. The experimental profiles deviate from SRIM predictions, ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 468.7pt, "indicating temperature-dependent He mobility. In the pre-damaged sample, the He profile is ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 489.4pt, "slightly shallower, with a dominant peak near 944 nm, closely matching the SRIM-predicted ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 510.1pt, "He-ion profile. By contrast, when implanted alone at RT or 750 °C, the dominant peak occurs ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 530.8pt, "deeper, at ~960 nm, than the SRIM prediction. These results highlight the combined influence ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 551.5pt, "of temperature and SiC matrix condition on He transport. The observed partial redistribution of ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 572.14pt, "He toward shallower depths may be linked to excess vacancy concentrations just below the ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 592.84pt, "damage peak. Such vacancies likely arise from forward-scattered recoils that become ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 613.54pt, "interstitials, leaving behind vacancy-rich zones capable of trapping helium. The apparent higher ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 634.24pt, "He concentration near the end of the range is likely an artefact caused by C recoil ions entering ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 654.94pt, "the detector, due to ion beam energies exceeding the optimal range for the entrance foil. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.86pt, 683.68pt, "Helium-Induced Microstructural Evolution at Elevated Temperature ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.86pt, 704.4pt, "Helium implantation at 750 °C leads to pronounced microstructural changes in sintered α-SiC, ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 725.1pt, "as observed through conventional TEM analysis of transverse FIB-prepared foils (Fig. 2). The ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 745.8pt, "implanted samples exhibit well-defined helium platelets exceeding 20 nm in length (marked ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 766.5pt, "with red arrows), along with nanocracks up to 120 nm, highlighted by yellow arrows in Fig. 2f. ")
]

