#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(513.36pt, 790.2pt, "12 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.86pt, 82.08pt, "Overall, the DBS results are in strong agreement with TEM observations. High-temperature He ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 102.78pt, "implantation alone tends to produce fewer but larger defects, such as extended platelets or ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 123.48pt, "bubbles. In contrast, pre-damaging the material via C implantation alters the defect evolution ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 144.2pt, "pathway, promoting the formation of smaller, more numerous vacancy-type defects that ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 164.9pt, "effectively trap helium and inhibit the development of larger defect structures. The co-")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 185.6pt, "implanted sample exhibits a higher degree of positron trapping than the He-only sample, ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 206.3pt, "indicating a greater population of small vacancy clusters. This interpretation is further ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 227pt, "corroborated by strain analysis and simulation results, reinforcing the role of pre-damage in ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 247.7pt, "tailoring the defect landscape ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(214.88pt, 243.2pt, "55")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(222.92pt, 247.7pt, ". ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.86pt, 280.4pt, "Discussion ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.86pt, 301.1pt, "The results demonstrate that pre-damage engineering in Sintered α-SiC significantly alters ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 321.8pt, "helium-induced defect evolution. Instead of forming extended defects such as platelets and ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 342.44pt, "nanocracks, the microstructure transitions toward stable, sub-nanometer helium-vacancy ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 363.14pt, "clusters. This transformation is driven by the presence of pre-existing voids and vacancy ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 383.84pt, "clusters, introduced via controlled carbon self-ion irradiation, which act as efficient sinks for ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 404.54pt, "both interstitials and helium atoms. As shown in Fig. 1, helium implanted at 750 °C into ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 425.26pt, "undamaged α-SiC undergoes limited redistribution and readily nucleates extended defects, most ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 445.96pt, "notably, nanocracks and platelets localized near the peak helium concentration (~930 nm), as ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 466.66pt, "observed in Figs. 3 a-g. In contrast, samples that underwent co-irradiation with carbon ions at ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 487.36pt, "doses of 0.25-0.5 dpa exhibit a marked shift in helium migration toward deeper regions ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 508.06pt, "(~1120 nm), aligning with the carbon-induced damage peak. This behavior confirms ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 528.76pt, "preferential helium trapping in defect-rich zones. ")
