  #line-at(70.86pt, 395.24pt, "temperature range of 50-713 K. ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 424pt, "In these studies, the suppression of newly formed large vacancy clusters was attributed to the ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 444.7pt, "presence of pre-existing damage, though the underlying mechanism remained unclear. In this ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 465.4pt, "work, we propose a mechanism for void shrinkage based on the interaction of newly generated ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 486.1pt, "interstitials and Frenkel pairs with pre-existing voids (see Supplementary Movie 1). Fig. 12 ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 506.8pt, "illustrates the microstructural evolution of defects during both the intermediate and final stages ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 527.5pt, "of the cascade process, highlighting the dynamic interplay between cascade-induced defects ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 548.2pt, "and pre-existing void structures. Various types of defects are generated, including Carbon ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 568.9pt, "vacancies (Vc), silicon vacancies (V")
