  #line-at(70.86pt, 131.48pt, "The correlation between simulation results and experimental observations highlights the crucial ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 152.18pt, "role of pre-existing damage in governing He-induced defect evolution in α-SiC. The behavior ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 172.88pt, "of helium in the matrix, with or without pre-damage, can be described as follows: During He ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 193.58pt, "implantation into pre-irradiated samples, collision cascades from incoming ions overlap with ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 214.28pt, "pre-existing voids. These voids serve as efficient sinks for interstitials, leading to localized void ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 234.98pt, "shrinkage (Fig. 12) and altering the cascade recombination dynamics. As a result, numerous ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 255.68pt, "small vacancy clusters form near the cascade core. These clusters serve as distributed trapping ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 276.38pt, "sites for helium, promoting a more spatially diffuse defect distribution. For instance, at ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 297.08pt, "0.36 dpa, He bubbles are spread across a ~400 nm region, in contrast to the ~100 nm localization ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 317.78pt, "observed in undamaged samples, where helium accumulation leads to platelet and nanocrack ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 338.48pt, "formation. This spatial broadening is reflected in the wider strain profiles shown in Fig. 9. Pre-")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 359.18pt, "existing vacancy clusters thus play dual roles: (1) acting as sinks for mobile interstitials, and ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 379.88pt, "(2) serving as nucleation sites for helium trapping. The local He concentration in these small ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 400.58pt, "clusters remains below the threshold for platelet formation. Simulations show enhanced helium ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 421.3pt, "binding energies in smaller vacancy clusters, suggesting thermodynamic stabilization of ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 442pt, "dispersed nanobubbles over platelet formation. In contrast, in undamaged samples, cascade-")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 462.7pt, "induced clustering tends to produce larger vacancy aggregates. At high irradiation temperatures, ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 483.4pt, "enhanced mobility allows helium atoms to overfill these large clusters (He/vacancy ratio >1), ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 504.1pt, "triggering platelet nucleation and coalescence into over-pressurized platelets and eventually ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 524.8pt, "nanocracks (Fig. 2). Therefore, maintaining a high density of small, isolated vacancy clusters ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 545.5pt, "is key to suppressing extended defect growth. These findings underscore the potential of defect ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 566.14pt, "engineering to control the helium defect landscape. Low-dose pre-damage favors distributed ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 586.84pt, "He bubble formation, while higher-dose pre-damage leads to uniform arrays of sub-nanometer ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 607.54pt, "He bubbles with no evidence of platelets or cracks. This approach fundamentally alters helium ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 628.24pt, "behavior and enhances the radiation tolerance of α-SiC. ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 656.98pt, "Although demonstrated here in α-SiC, the concept of defect landscape engineering is broadly ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 677.68pt, "applicable to a wide class of radiation-sensitive ceramics. Many high-performance ceramics ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 698.4pt, "used in nuclear, fusion, and aerospace environments, including carbides (ZrC, TiC, B")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
