  #line-at(70.86pt, 82.08pt, "independent lever for redirecting He transport and clustering, independent of grain size, phase ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 102.78pt, "composition, or interface density. In systems where compositional modification is impractical ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 123.48pt, "due to manufacturing constraints or qualification requirements, pre-damage engineering can be ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 144.2pt, "implemented through controlled ion implantation, neutron irradiation, or even additive ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 164.9pt, "manufacturing routes that introduce vacancy-rich regions during processing. The mechanistic ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 185.6pt, "principles identified here, vacancy clusters as dual-function helium traps and cascade sinks, are ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 206.3pt, "general and scalable, offering a versatile design pathway for extending the lifetime and ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 227pt, "reliability of ceramic components across multiple extreme-environment applications. ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 259.7pt, "This work demonstrates that deliberately engineered vacancy landscapes can fundamentally ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 280.4pt, "reshape He defect evolution in ceramics. By stabilizing uniformly dispersed nanobubbles and ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 301.1pt, "suppressing extended defect formation, defect landscape engineering provides a general, ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 321.8pt, "composition-independent strategy for improving radiation tolerance. The approach reframes ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 342.44pt, "defect control in ceramics from a passive property to an actively tunable design parameter, ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 363.14pt, "enabling the creation of next-generation materials capable of sustained performance in the ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 383.84pt, "harshest operational environments. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.86pt, 416.56pt, "Materials and methods ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 439.24pt, "Ion Distribution and Implantation Strategy ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.86pt, 460pt, "To investigate the interaction of helium with pre-existing damage, sintered α-SiC samples were ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 480.7pt, "subjected to a series of controlled ion irradiations. Carbon self-ion irradiation was performed at ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 501.4pt, "room temperature using 1080 keV C ions at fluences of 2 × 10¹⁵ ions/cm² and 4 × 10¹⁵ ions/cm², ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 522.1pt, "resulting in displacement damage levels of approximately 0.25 dpa and 0.5 dpa, respectively. ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 542.8pt, "The use of carbon as a self-ion ensured no contamination by foreign elements and allowed ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 563.5pt, "precise control over defect generation; moreover, the energy is relevant to C recoil energies ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 584.14pt, "produced in SiC by fusion neutrons. Following C irradiation, the same samples were implanted ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 604.84pt, "with helium ions at 300 keV to a fluence of 1 × 10")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
