  #line-at(258.56pt, 123.48pt, " ions/cm² fluence, with their maxima located deeper, ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 144.2pt, "around 1120 nm. To promote helium trapping in vacancy-rich regions while minimizing direct ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 164.9pt, "interaction with implanted carbon, the C implantation profile was designed to peak deeper than ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 185.6pt, "the He profile, so that migrating helium atoms primarily encounter pre-existing vacancy clusters ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 206.3pt, "rather than the dilute implanted C atoms. This intentional offset ensures that helium atoms ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 227pt, "primarily interact with damaged structures rather than with implanted carbon atoms themselves. ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 247.7pt, "As shown in Fig.  15, this design enables spatial separation between helium concentration and ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 268.4pt, "carbon content, thereby isolating the role of pre-existing damage in modifying helium behavior. ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 289.1pt, "This controlled implantation strategy enables a systematic study of how irradiation-induced ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 309.8pt, "defects influence helium trapping, diffusion, and cluster evolution in SiC. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.86pt, 367.16pt, "Helium Depth Profiling via ERDA ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.86pt, 387.86pt, "To characterize the in-depth distribution of helium, Elastic Recoil Detection Analysis (ERDA) ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 408.56pt, "was conducted using a 48 MeV Cl⁷⁺ ion beam. The incident beam was aligned at a 75° angle ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 429.28pt, "relative to the sample normal, with a scattering angle of 30°, covering an analysis area of ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 449.98pt, "approximately 2 × 2 mm². Recoiled atoms and scattered ions were detected using a Bragg ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 470.68pt, "Ionization Chamber (BIC), which enables both energy resolution and atomic number (Z) ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 491.38pt, "identification. Helium recoils were detected by a dedicated solid-state detector positioned at a ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 512.08pt, "40° scattering angle. A 25 μm Kapton foil was placed in front of this detector to block heavier ")
  #line-at(70.86pt, 532.78pt, "recoils and scattered ions, ensuring selective helium detection. Although this setup reduces ")
